me":"Turkic","termine":"","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"ar","nome":"Arabic","termine":"خَلْق","traslitterazione":"ḵalq","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"Uncertain. Possibly from Old East Slavic калига (kaliga, “pilgrim's footwear”), from Byzantine Greek καλίγα (kalíga), from Latin caliga. Alternatively, from Turkic, either the same as Etymology 1 or via some Turkic language from Arabic خَلْق (ḵalq, “people”)."}]}